# Findings

## High — OpenCode palette certification contradicts the dispatch

Phase 1's `select_palette` requires `Music` and `Play / pause` on the same ANSI line and requires the title to be bold (`rows.filter(boldAt)`). The ordered work and acceptance checks repeat this as an “ANSI-confirmed bold” requirement. The dispatch explicitly forbids requiring either same-line placement or exact bold styling and says the subsequent canonical media transition plus convergence of both host UIs is authoritative proof that the command executed.

Revise the palette check to open the palette, type the exact unique `Music / Play / pause` query, and capture both the query and resulting palette without those layout/style gates. Keep the existing post-Enter canonical transition and two-host UI convergence as the execution proof. The emitted evidence should explicitly include the query (for example, `query=...`), rather than only `selected=<group>/<title>`.
